  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0119 database is used to store information about basketball games, players, and teams. It contains five tables: Actions, Game, Player, Team, and joined_drafted_all_players_original.\nThe Actions table stores information about individual player actions during a game, such as the number of minutes played, field goals made, and personal fouls committed. It has 21 columns, including primary keys for GameId and PlayerId, and foreign keys for GameId, PlayerId, and TeamId.\nThe Game table stores information about each game, such as the team scores, the date of the game, and the URL of the game video. It has 6 columns, including a primary key for GameId and foreign keys for Team1Id and Team2Id.\nThe Player table stores information about each player, such as their name and position. It has 2 columns, including a primary key for PlayerId.\nThe Team table stores information about each team, such as their name and the players on their roster. It has 2 columns, including a primary key for TeamId.\nThe joined_drafted_all_players_original table stores information about all players, including their age, draft year, and career statistics. It has 32 columns, including primary keys for ID and season, and foreign keys for ID, draft_g, and draft_year.\nOverall, the schemabench_0119 database is designed to provide a comprehensive and detailed view of basketball games, players, and teams. It is organized into five tables, each with its own unique columns and relationships, which work together to provide a complete picture of the data.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\nThe project involves developing a data management system for tracking and analyzing basketball match information from the National Basketball Association (NBA). This system will consist of a database capable of storing details about players, teams, and individual match actions.\n\n Objectives\nThe primary goal is to create a structured database that allows for efficient storage and retrieval of game data, player statistics, and team performances. The system will support the analysis of player actions and match results to aid in performance assessment and historical analysis.\n\n Stakeholders & Users\n- Stakeholders: NBA organizations, sports analysts, data scientists, and statisticians.\n- Users: Team managers, coaches, players, sports analysts, and technical staff.\n\n Functional Descriptions\n1. Game Information Management: Store details of each game, including participating teams, results, and the date of the match.\n2. Player Data Storage: Maintain a repository of player information, including names and identifiers.\n3. Team Data Storage: Store information about teams, including team names and identifiers.\n4. Action Tracking: Record player-specific actions during games, such as minutes played, points, rebounds, assists, and other performance metrics.\n5. Historical Data Analysis: Support the analysis of action counts and game outcomes for performance evaluations across different seasons.\n6. Integration with External Links: Store URLs associated with games for additional context or media links.\n\n Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Data Integrity: Ensure consistency and accuracy of the data, with foreign key constraints maintaining valid references between tables.\n- Scalability: Design the database to handle large volumes of data, accommodating historical records and ongoing updates.\n- Performance: Optimize queries and database operations to support fast retrieval of large datasets.\n- Security: Implement access control and ensure that sensitive data is protected against unauthorized access.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0119.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0119\nCREATE TABLE `Actions` (\n  `GameId` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `PlayerId` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `minutes_played` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `field_goals_made` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `personal_fouls` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `assists` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `rebounds` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `steals` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `blocks` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `turnovers` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `three_point_field_goals_made` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `free_throws_made` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `field_goal_percentage` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `three_point_percentage` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `free_throw_percentage` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `plus_minus` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `game_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`GameId`, `PlayerId`),\n  KEY `fk_game` (`GameId`),\n  KEY `fk_player` (`PlayerId`),\n  CONSTRAINT `Actions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`GameId`) REFERENCES `Game` (`GameId`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `Actions_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`PlayerId`) REFERENCES `Player` (`PlayerId`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Game` (\n  `GameId` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Team1Id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Team2Id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `team1_score` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `team2_score` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `video_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`GameId`),\n  KEY `fk_team1` (`Team1Id`),\n  KEY `fk_team2` (`Team2Id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `Game_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Team1Id`) REFERENCES `Team` (`TeamId`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `Game_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Team2Id`) REFERENCES `Team` (`TeamId`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Player` (\n  `PlayerId` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`PlayerId`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Team` (\n  `TeamId` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`TeamId`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `joined_drafted_all_players_original` (\n  `ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `season` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `draft_year` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `career_points` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `career_assists` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `career_rebounds` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `draft_g` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `draft_round` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `draft_pick` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `team` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `games_played` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `minutes_per_game` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `field_goal_percentage` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `three_point_percentage` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `free_throw_percentage` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `points_per_game` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `assists_per_game` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `rebounds_per_game` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `steals_per_game` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `blocks_per_game` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `turnovers_per_game` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `plus_minus` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `career_games` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `career_minutes` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `career_field_goals_made` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `career_three_point_field_goals_made` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `career_free_throws_made` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `career_field_goals_attempted` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `career_three_point_field_goals_attempted` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `career_free_throws_attempted` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `career_draft_year` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`ID`, `season`),\n  KEY `fk_draft_g` (`draft_g`),\n  CONSTRAINT `joined_drafted_all_players_original_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`ID`) REFERENCES `Player` (`PlayerId`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `joined_drafted_all_players_original_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`draft_g`) REFERENCES `Team` (`TeamId`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
